Z||000000||fldevel||06-28-2000||07:41 PM||||i have a set of 205/60R15 all the way around and was wondaring if i can put 225/60R15 on the rear  rims .. will they fit ?? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Terrybogin||06-28-2000||08:10 PM||||Cooter has 235/60-15's on the back of his car and it has no problems.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||06-28-2000||11:52 PM||||I have 225/60r15's on the back of my GT right now, fit perfect and looks great!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||06-29-2000||12:34 AM||||I've had wear problems using 225/60/15s on my 7" rear rims.  They wear in the center.  The last two sets of tires didn't last 6k miles per.  Should have learned my lesson the first time.  Needless to say I'm going back to the 215s.  It's kind of like changing the gearing when you step up a size.  You'll get better pull from the shorter tires.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-29-2000||09:27 AM||||Have you checked your air pressure lately?  Usually when a tire wears in the middle only, it's due to overinflation.  (Which is why the US is wearing in the middle only.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||fldevel||06-29-2000||12:17 PM||||i know theil fit in the wells was wondaring if they would fit on the rims ??  any tire experts out there ?<BR> <P>  sorry dident explain my question correctly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ...still gettin used to this forum stuff <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fldevel (edited 06-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||06-29-2000||12:29 PM||||They should fit....<P>If the tires are wearing in the middle then let some air out of them....||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||06-29-2000||12:33 PM||||225s will fit on the rim... not part of your question but Don't go any larger than a 225 on a 7" wheel.  that leaves almost 1" on either side of the tire unsupported. unsupported tires will cause a higher slip angle.. leading to crappy hard corner handling, and will cause the car to sway in emergency braking.  <P>225/25.4-7/2=.929" <BR>tire section width/25.4(mm-in)-wheel width/2(number of sideswalls)=inches unsupported  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||06-29-2000||10:07 PM||||I've messed around with pressures for too long.  I could run the tires on 10psi and they would still wear in the middle.  The actual increase of tire width on the road is 1cm per tire.  That's not enough to make me want to shell out $160 for new back tires every two months.  I know others have been running that size for a while with no problems, but they probably aren't running as soft of compound as me.  I also think the taller sidewalls make the car look like a goofy streetrod  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
